    idealAnswer: 'Naïve RAG embeds documents, performs top-k cosine similarity search, and concatenates retrieved chunks into an LLM prompt.\n\nFailure Modes:\n1. Low Precision / Irrelevant Retrieval: Dense embeddings struggle with exact keywords, error codes, and entity names.\n2. Lost in the Middle: LLMs attend strongly to start and end of context windows, ignoring relevant information placed in middle chunks.\n3. Hallucination from Noise: Non-relevant retrieved context induces hallucinations.\n\nAdvanced / Modular RAG Solutions:\n1. Pre-Retrieval: Query expansion (HyDE - Hypothetical Document Embeddings), query rewriting.\n2. Hybrid Search: Dense vector retrieval combined with sparse BM25 via Reciprocal Rank Fusion (RRF).\n3. Post-Retrieval: Cross-Encoder Reranker (Cohere / BGE-Reranker) selecting top 3 most precise chunks, followed by contextual compression.',
