    interviewerPrompt: 'What is a Feature Store (e.g. Feast), and how does it prevent Training-Serving Skew?',
    idealAnswer: 'A Feature Store is a centralized repository managing feature definitions, storage, and access.\n\nTraining-Serving Skew Problem:\nOccurs when features calculated during offline model training differ from features computed in real time during live online inference (e.g. calculating rolling 30-day average transaction count via different SQL logic in batch vs Python in production).\n\nFeature Store Dual Architecture:\n1. Offline Store (Snowflake / BigQuery / Parquet on S3): Stores historical feature values. Provides point-in-time "time-travel" joins ensuring no future data leakage during training set creation.\n2. Online Store (Redis / DynamoDB): Ultra-low-latency key-value store serving latest feature values (<10ms) to real-time inference APIs.\nBoth stores derive from identical declarative feature definitions, eliminating logic skew.',
