    idealAnswer: 'Individual client inference requests arrive asynchronously at unpredictable millisecond intervals. Running GPU inference on single-item batches (batch size = 1) leaves GPU compute cores heavily underutilized (<15% utilization).\n\nDynamic Batching Mechanism:\nTriton buffers incoming individual requests on the server side into a queue for a configurable micro-window (e.g. max_queue_delay_microseconds = 5000):\n1. As soon as either `max_batch_size` (e.g. 32) is reached OR the timeout expires, the requests are assembled into a single contiguous tensor batch.\n2. GPU executes one parallel matrix operation across all 32 items.\n3. Results are disaggregated and returned to respective client connections.\nIncreases overall inference throughput by 5–10x with negligible latency impact.',
